# Supply Chain Command Center

One-click supply chain risk dashboard (demo POC). Configure suppliers, parts, and scenarios in YAML, then run a full analysis pipeline from the UI or API.

**Demo data only** — synthetic suppliers and parts for illustration, not Maruti Suzuki proprietary information.

## Features

### UI (after **Run analysis**)

| Area | What you get |
|------|----------------|
| **Home** | Landing page, quick links, interactive 3D SUV hero (community Vitara Brezza model) |
| **Command center** | KPIs, ops signals, live news ticker, risks, recommendations — click critical items for **why** details |
| **AI & twin** | AI model fleet status and digital-twin plant telemetry |
| **Brief & strategy** | Company profile, SWOT & PESTLE with citations |
| **Parts catalog** | Full BOM-style list with main supplier and alternates |
| **Suppliers** | Directory plus sourcing matrix and mitigation playbooks |
| **Fear & Greed** | Sentiment index (0–100) for MSIL and each supplier |
| **Scenario lab** | 11 disruption scenarios, 3 strategies, Monte Carlo, matrix view |
| **Why panel** | TOPSIS ranks and allocation rationale (opens from parts / command center) |

Pipeline: ingest (World Bank, GDELT, RSS, optional FRED) → country/commodity/supplier risk → MCDM (TOPSIS) → SimPy scenarios → recommendations → DuckDB + JSON snapshot.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Backend | Python 3.11+, FastAPI, uvicorn |
| Database | DuckDB (`data/analytics.duckdb`) |
| Analytics | NumPy, SimPy, rule-based news classification |
| Frontend | React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Three.js |
| Data | World Bank & GDELT (no key), RSS; optional FRED / NewsData via `.env` |

## Prerequisites

- Python 3.11+
- Node.js 20+
- (Optional) [FRED API key](https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys) for richer commodity series

> **Windows:** `make` is not installed by default. Use **`.\tasks.ps1`** (same targets as `Makefile`). Optional: `winget install GnuWin32.Make` or Git Bash.

## Quick start (Windows / PowerShell)

### 1. Install

```powershell
cd e:\Amit\MarutiSuzuki
.\tasks.ps1 install
.\tasks.ps1 migrate
```

### 2. Run (two terminals from **repo root**)

```powershell
# Terminal 1 — API
.\tasks.ps1 backend

# Terminal 2 — UI
.\tasks.ps1 frontend
```

| URL | Service |
|-----|---------|
| http://localhost:5173 | React UI |
| http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs | API (Swagger) |

Open the UI and click **Run analysis**. The first run may take 15–30 seconds while external APIs and caches warm up.

### Troubleshooting (Windows)

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `tasks.ps1` not recognized | Run from **repo root** (`e:\Amit\MarutiSuzuki`), not only inside `frontend\`. From `frontend\`, use `.\tasks.ps1 frontend` (forwards to root). |
| `WinError 10013` / port in use on **8000** | `.\tasks.ps1 backend-stop` then `.\tasks.ps1 backend` |
| UI port **5173** stuck | `.\tasks.ps1 frontend-stop` then `.\tasks.ps1 frontend` |
| Change ports | Copy `.env.example` → `.env`, set `API_PORT=8010` and/or `$env:VITE_PORT = 5174` before starting |
| Backend import errors after edits | Stop backend (`backend-stop`), start again — avoid multiple uvicorn instances |

List all commands: `.\tasks.ps1 help`

### 3. Optional environment

Copy `.env.example` to `.env`:

```env
API_PORT=8000
FRED_API_KEY=
NEWSDATA_API_KEY=
ENABLE_HF_CLASSIFIER=false
CONFIG_DIR=config
DATA_DIR=data
```

### Manual commands (no tasks.ps1)

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\pip install -e ".[dev]"
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m backend.db.migrate
cd frontend; npm install; cd ..
.\.venv\Scripts\uvicorn backend.main:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
# other terminal:
cd frontend; npm run dev
```

## Configuration

Business rules live in [`config/`](config/) — edit YAML only for typical tuning:

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `suppliers.yaml` | 33+ suppliers with trust tiers and IndiaMART category URLs |
| `supplier_trust.yaml` | Trust tier definitions |
| `parts.yaml` / `parts_extra.yaml` | Automotive parts (braking, powertrain, electrical, etc.) |
| `maruti_company.yaml` | Maruti Suzuki India company brief |
| `strategic_analysis.yaml` | SWOT & PESTLE for MSIL and partner archetypes |
| `plants.yaml` | Plant list for digital twin |
| `mcdm.yaml` | Ranking criteria and weights |
| `thresholds.yaml` | Risk and dual-source thresholds |
| `scenarios.yaml` | Disruption shocks for simulation |
| `data_sources.yaml` | Countries, indicators, GDELT queries, RSS URLs |
| `news_keywords.yaml` | Rule-based news severity taxonomy |

See [`docs/CONFIG_GUIDE.md`](docs/CONFIG_GUIDE.md) and [`docs/DATA_SOURCES.md`](docs/DATA_SOURCES.md).

## API

Interactive docs: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `POST` | `/api/run-analysis` | Run full pipeline; returns snapshot JSON |
| `GET` | `/api/snapshot/latest` | Latest snapshot (404 if never run) |
| `GET` | `/api/health/data-sources` | Per-provider ingest health |
| `GET` | `/api/health` | Liveness |
| `GET` | `/api/company/profile` | Company brief |
| `GET` | `/api/company/strategic` | SWOT & PESTLE |
| `GET` | `/api/parts/catalog` | Parts by category |
| `GET` | `/api/parts/catalog/enriched` | Parts with post-run risk overlays |
| `GET` | `/api/sourcing/matrix` | Main supplier, alternates, mitigation |
| `GET` | `/api/sentiment/fear-greed` | Fear & Greed indices |
| `GET` | `/api/suppliers/catalog` | Supplier directory |
| `GET` | `/api/scenarios/catalog` | Scenario catalog metadata |

## Project layout

```
backend/          # FastAPI, ingestion, analytics, DuckDB
frontend/         # React UI (frontend/tasks.ps1 forwards to root tasks.ps1)
config/           # YAML business config
data/             # DuckDB, cache, snapshots (gitignored)
e2e/              # Playwright tests
scripts/          # Security audit, plugin helpers
tasks.ps1         # Windows task runner
docs/             # Architecture and config guides
```

## Tests and quality

Use **`.\tasks.ps1 <target>`** on Windows, or **`make <target>`** if GNU Make is installed.

| Target | What it does |
|--------|----------------|
| `.\tasks.ps1 test` | Backend unit + integration tests (`pytest`) |
| `.\tasks.ps1 test-e2e` | Playwright: UI **Run analysis** flow |
| `.\tasks.ps1 audit` | `pip-audit` + `npm audit` |
| `.\tasks.ps1 pins` | Print key dependency versions |
| `.\tasks.ps1 health` | CLI data-source ingest check |
| `.\tasks.ps1 plugin-check` | Audit + pins + tests + E2E |

```powershell
.\tasks.ps1 test
.\tasks.ps1 help
```

## Cursor plugins (optional)

